seek new solutions?

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:23.434
-I-I don't know what the hell's
going on in this world.

00:06:23.434 --> 00:06:25.467
I'm not even sure
if I understood that question.

00:06:25.467 --> 00:06:27.133
[ Laughter ]
-Well...

00:06:31.667 --> 00:06:33.634
When you've lost Kid Rock...

00:06:33.634 --> 00:06:35.000
[ Laughter ]

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:38.334
The best part is they laugh
about it like it's a joke,

00:06:38.334 --> 00:06:39.868
but then Tucker doubles down
and says,

00:06:39.868 --> 00:06:42.300
"No, seriously,
why not consider it?"

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:43.968
Hell, why stop
at red light therapy?

00:06:43.968 --> 00:06:46.300
Maybe in addition to light,
your testicles need air,

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:47.634
which we could generate using...

00:06:47.634 --> 00:06:48.634
-Windmills.

00:06:48.634 --> 00:06:49.634
-And...

00:06:49.634 --> 00:06:50.968
[ Laughter ]

00:06:50.968 --> 00:06:54.133
Also, even if there was
some sort of massive

00:06:54.133 --> 00:06:56.000
global testosterone crisis,

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:58.868
is it already time to resort
to tanning your balls?

00:06:58.868 --> 00:07:01.901
Nothing is crazier than
a conservative's second idea.

00:07:01.901 --> 00:07:04.467
"I don't trust vaccines,
but I'll eat some horse paste."

00:07:04.467 --> 00:07:07.801
Are there ever solutions
somewhere between Plan A

00:07:07.801 --> 00:07:09.968
and the craziest [bleep]
you've ever heard?

00:07:09.968 --> 00:07:11.634
It's like if someone said,
"There's a bird in the house,"

00:07:11.634 --> 00:07:12.667
and you said, "Open a window,"

00:07:12.667 --> 00:07:14.033
and they said,
"That didn't work,"

00:07:14.033 --> 00:07:15.534
